  "live_records": {
    "q-166825": {
      "dom_id": "question-166825",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Expressed as an improper fraction, Catherine has$\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$liters of alcohol.",
      "worked_solution": "The exact amount of alcohol is ${(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}$ liters.\n\nWriting ${(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}$ with multiplication signs, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} & ={{\\frac{8}{3}\\times \\frac{8}{3}}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\times 8}{3\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}=\\frac{64}{9}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
