    "q-166830": {
      "dom_id": "question-166830",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Catherine sold $6$ identical bottles of perfume, for which she received a total of $$90.33.$ Estimate the price of each bottle by rounding the amount of money Catherine received to the nearest dollar.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The approximate price for each bottle is $\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
      "worked_solution": "To estimate the price of each of the $6$ perfumes, we need to find an approximation for $90.33÷6.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n90.33\\to 90\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $90$ by $6$ as usual:\n\n$$\n90÷6=15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the approximate price for each bottle is $$15.$",
